The q-points are passed in the qpts list. If qplot is\nset to True then qpts is expected to be a list of list|tuple of length 4.\nWhere the first three elements are the coordinates of the q-point in units\nof 2pi/alat and the last element is the weight of the q-point. if qplot is\nset to False then qpts is expected to be a simple list of length 4 (single\nq-point). Finally if ldisp is set to True, the above is discarded and the\nq-points are read from the nq1, nq2, nq3 cards in the input_data dictionary.', 'title': 'ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_ph', 'url': 'https://docs.ase-lib.org/ase/calculators/espresso.html#ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_ph', 'source': 'ase', 'metadata': {'source': 'ase', 'module': 'ase.calculators.espresso', 'qualified_name': 'ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_ph', 'kind': 'function', 'name': 'write_espresso_ph', 'class': None, 'function': 'write_espresso_ph', 'chunk_index': 0, 'num_chunks': 2}, 'score': 5.893914222717285, 'vector_score': 0.5237230658531189, 'bm25_score': 33.568246450456165, 'rerank_score': 5.893914222717285}, {'text': '[ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in]\nCompared to Γ-point-only calculations without this optimization\n(i.e. with kpts=(1, 1, 1) ), the memory and CPU requirements\nare typically reduced by half. If kpts is a dict, it will either be interpreted as a path\nin the Brillouin zone (*) if it contains the ‘path’ keyword,\notherwise it is converted to a Monkhorst-Pack grid (**). If kpts is a NumPy array, the raw k-points will be passed to\nQuantum Espresso as given in the array (in crystal coordinates). Must be of shape (n_kpts, 4). The fourth column contains the\nk-point weights. (*) see ase.dft.kpoints.bandpath\n(**) see ase.calculators.calculator.kpts2sizeandoffsets koffset ( ( int , int , int ) ) – Offset of kpoints in each direction. Must be 0 (no offset) or\n1 (half grid offset). Setting to True is equivalent to (1, 1, 1).', 'title': 'ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in', 'url': 'https://docs.ase-lib.org/ase/io/formatoptions.html#ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in', 'source': 'ase', 'metadata': {'source': 'ase', 'module': 'ase.io.formatoptions', 'qualified_name': 'ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in', 'kind': 'function', 'name': 'write_espresso_in', 'class': None, 'function': 'write_espresso_in', 'chunk_index': 3, 'num_chunks': 5}, 'score': 4.990489959716797, 'vector_score': 0.5364865660667419, 'bm25_score': 22.169972927437673, 'rerank_score': 4.990489959716797}, {'text': '[ase.io.espresso.write_fortran_namelist]\nfunction ase.io.espresso.write_fortran_namelist\n\nase.io.espresso. write_fortran_namelist ( fd , input_data = None , binary = None , additional_cards = None , ** kwargs ) → None [source] #\n\nFunction which writes input for simple espresso binaries.\nList of supported binaries are in the espresso_keys.py file.\nNon-exhaustive list (to complete)\n\nNote: “EOF” is appended at the end of the file.\n( https://lists.quantum-espresso.org/pipermail/users/2020-November/046269.html )\n\nAdditional fields are written ‘as is’ in the input file. It is expected\nto be a string or a list of strings.', 'title': 'ase.io.espresso.write_fortran_namelist', 'url': 'https://docs.ase-lib.org/ase/calculators/espresso.html#ase.io.espresso.write_fortran_namelist', 'source': 'ase', 'metadata': {'source': 'ase', 'module': 'ase.calculators.espresso', 'qualified_name': 'ase.io.espresso.write_fortran_namelist', 'kind': 'function', 'name': 'write_fortran_namelist', 'class': None, 'function': 'write_fortran_namelist', 'chunk_index': 0, 'num_chunks': 2}, 'score': 4.989434719085693, 'vector_score': 0.5661987066268921, 'bm25_score': 30.835719419420226, 'rerank_score': 4.989434719085693}, {'text': '[ase.io.espresso.read_espresso_in]\nfunction ase.io.espresso.read_espresso_in\n\nase.io.espresso. read_espresso_in ( fileobj ) [source] #\n\nParse a Quantum ESPRESSO input files, ‘.in’, ‘.pwi’.\n\nESPRESSO inputs are generally a fortran-namelist format with custom\nblocks of data. The namelist is parsed as a dict and an atoms object\nis constructed from the included information.\n\nParameters : fileobj ( file | str ) – A file-like object that supports line iteration with the contents\nof the input file, or a filename. Returns : atoms – Structure defined in the input file. Return type : Atoms Raises : KeyError – Raised for missing keys that are required to process the file', 'title': 'ase.io.espresso.read_espresso_in', 'url': 'https://docs.ase-lib.org/ase/io/formatoptions.html#ase.io.espresso.read_espresso_in', 'source': 'ase', 'metadata': {'source': 'ase', 'module': 'ase.io.formatoptions', 'qualified_name': 'ase.io.espresso.read_espresso_in', 'kind': 'function', 'name': 'read_espresso_in', 'class': None, 'function': 'read_espresso_in', 'chunk_index': 0, 'num_chunks': 1}, 'score': 3.485872268676758, 'vector_score': 0.5035669803619385, 'bm25_score': 28.93245482809544, 'rerank_score': 3.485872268676758}]}

